WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.460 --> 00:00:03.460
Knight Lautrec looks out for himself.

00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:06.760
If we are to judge him, then we should count our own sins first.

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:09.360
You, who invades for humanity.

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:12.500
You, who kills, simply because something is in your way,

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:14.880
or because they have something important to you.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:19.580
Helm of Lautrec the Embraced, representing the goddess Fina's love.

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:22.360
During his solitude, he forsook everything,

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:25.100
for he believed in the goddess' love for him.

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:31.800
Ring of Favor and Protection, granted by Fina, known in legend to possess fateful beauty.

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:34.360
The ring breaks, if ever removed.

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:38.560
Armor of Lautrec the Embraced, representing the goddess Fina's love.

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:42.300
The goddess' arms wrap around it, as if to embrace the wearer.

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:47.140
The goddess Fina seems more sinister than you'd expect from a goddess of love.

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:51.780
She appears to a man who has forsaken everything, who will commit atrocities to serve

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:55.000
Her ring of protection breaks if you abandon her.

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:58.360
The armor wraps its arms around you, clinging to the wearer.

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:00.540
Is it a reminder of her love,

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:02.920
or to remind you, that you are hers?

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:04.680
We know her love is fateful

00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:07.700
If you're hers, you are well and truly a part of her design.

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:10.560
Whatever goal she has, are your's as well.

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:14.740
So did Fina really love him, deeply and personally?

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:16.400
It's possible.

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:19.080
Interactions between the gods and the humans are quite common.

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:22.820
It's also possible that the man is simply within a religious delusion.

00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:26.980
We first encounter Knight Lautrec in a cell within the undead Church.

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:30.240
Why a Church has a cell is a story in and of itself,

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:33.160
as is the story of how Lautrec came to be trapped there.

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:36.660
It could have something to do with the Firekeeper soul down below,

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:38.740
or perhaps Oswald the Pardoner.

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:40.060
Maybe both.

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:43.540
For if anyone is drenched in sin it's Lautrec.

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:46.040
And his desire for more humanity is clear

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:47.960
Even Patches speaks of it.

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:52.160
It comes are no surprise then that Lautrec sets his sight on a harmless Firekeeper.

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:56.340
Firekeeper's are corporeal manifestations of the bonfires they keep.

00:01:56.660 --> 00:01:59.360
Their souls are a draw for humanity offered to the bonfire.

00:01:59.620 --> 00:02:02.500
And as such their souls are gnawed by infinite humanity.

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:05.620
It's clear that this isn't a fate that the Firekeeper enjoys.

00:02:05.740 --> 00:02:09.640
Since she expresses that she wishes for the curse of the undead to be lifted

00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:11.860
So that she may die as a human.

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:14.940
Her tongue was cut out so she could not complain.

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:19.240
And her bloodstained skirt implies she was maimed so that she may not escape.

00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:24.220
Yet, despite this she expresses a desire to fulfill her fate as a Firekeeper.

00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:26.920
To a man who desires humanity,

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:29.220
whether for his goddess or for himself.

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:31.880
A Firekeepers soul is quite a prize.

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:40.500
Lautrec escapes with the Firekeeper's soul,

00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:44.740
whether he desires it for himself as a trophy or for his goddess is unclear.

00:02:45.080 --> 00:02:48.560
Yet, you and many other parallel Undead, track him down

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:50.620
and invade his world.

00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:55.380
"So,

00:02:55.840 --> 00:02:57.420
here we go again.

00:02:57.420 --> 00:03:02.480
How many times will these lambs rush to slaughter?"

00:03:17.820 --> 00:03:19.900
"Lets get it over with!"

00:03:56.760 --> 00:03:58.880
This is the end of Knight Lautrec.

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:01.700
Whatever his designs were, whatever the goddess wanted

00:04:02.020 --> 00:04:03.000
It died with him.

00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:06.740
So, is it worth restoring the Firekeeper?

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:09.760
Or will you give in to the same temptations as Lautrec?

00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:12.980
Who wants to go Hollow, after all?

